From 77a5a58b17a6ad4c3fe9a9e824dde7551687c608 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrei-Alexandru Bleortu <me@andrei-z.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 14:53:21 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] RADIUS client: Frame RADIUS/TLS messages by their length

RADIUS over TLS is a byte stream (RFC 6614, 3.4): a decrypted chunk can
hold several RADIUS messages or part of one. radius_client_receive()
took each chunk as one message, so a second response in it was dropped
("Ignored N extra bytes after RADIUS message") and a message split over
two chunks was rejected ("Invalid message length").

Collect the decrypted data per connection and process every complete
message by its Length field, keeping the rest for the next chunk. The
message processing moves to radius_client_handle_msg() so the stream
and the UDP paths share it.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Andrei-Alexandru Bleortu <me@andrei-z.com>
---
